description=The TID thesaurus models genre concepts as SKOS concepts 
                                     organised in hierarchical and associative structures. It enables 
                                     semantic interoperability across manuscript catalogues, bibliographic 
                                     datasets, and image-based representations described in the IMAGO ontology.
introduction=The IMAGO Thesaurus of Genres (TID) is a controlled vocabulary developed within the IMAGO project to support the semantic description and classification of literary genres found in Middle Ages and Renaissance manuscripts and early printed editions.

The thesaurus provides a structured and interoperable framework for identifying, annotating, and relating genre concepts in geographic latin works datasets, with particular attention to genres documented in the IMAGO knowledge base.
